{% comment %}
  Renders one horizontally looping row of review cards.

  This snippet owns the loop and nothing else: it lays the cards out twice, gives
  the row its direction and speed, and leaves the look of a card entirely to
  snippets/review-card.liquid. Both rows of a section are this one snippet with
  different arguments, so there is a single copy of the markup no matter how many
  rows a page ends up with.

  Two copies of the card list are rendered, which is what makes the loop
  seamless: the track slides by exactly one copy's width and restarts on an
  identical frame. assets/reviews-marquee.js appends further copies when the
  cards do not fill the row and replaces the estimated duration below with one
  measured from the real card widths — but the row already loops, at close to the
  right speed, without it.

  Requires assets/component-review-marquee.css.

  Accepts:
  - reviews:     {Array} Blocks (or any objects exposing the same `settings`)
    to render. Required.
  - row_map:     {Array} One entry per review, holding the row each belongs to.
    Omit to put every review in this row. (optional)
  - row_key:     {String} The row_map value this row claims. (optional)
  - direction:   {String} 'left' (default) or 'right'. (optional)
  - speed:       {Number} Scroll speed in pixels per second. Default 40.
    (optional)
  - card_width:  {Number} Card width in px, used only to estimate the duration
    before JS measures. Default 320. (optional)
  - card_gap:    {Number} Space between cards in px, same purpose. Default 20.
    (optional)
  - row_label:   {String} Accessible name for the list of reviews. (optional)
  - quote_marks: {Boolean} Passed through to each card. (optional)
  - clamp:       {Boolean} Passed through to each card. (optional)
  - eager:       {Boolean} true loads the first few avatars eagerly. Pass it for
    a row that sits above the fold. (optional)

  Usage:
    render 'reviews-marquee-row', reviews: review_blocks, row_map: row_map,
      row_key: 't', direction: 'left', speed: 40
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign row_direction = direction | default: 'left'
  assign row_speed = speed | default: 40 | at_least: 1
  assign estimate_width = card_width | default: 320
  assign estimate_gap = card_gap | default: 20

  comment
    Which of the passed reviews belong to this row. Counted up front because the
    duration estimate needs the total, and because a row that matched nothing
    must not render an empty, still-animating track.
  endcomment
  assign row_count = 0
  for review in reviews
    if row_map == blank or row_key == blank
      assign row_count = row_count | plus: 1
    elsif row_map[forloop.index0] == row_key
      assign row_count = row_count | plus: 1
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    Distance one copy of the cards covers, in px, and therefore how long a lap
    takes at the requested px/s. This only has to be close: the script replaces
    it with the measured value as soon as it runs.
  endcomment
  assign card_span = estimate_width | plus: estimate_gap
  assign group_span = card_span | times: row_count
  assign row_duration = group_span | times: 1.0 | divided_by: row_speed | round: 2
  assign row_duration = row_duration | at_least: 1
-%}

{%- if row_count > 0 -%}
  <div
    class="review-marquee__row{% if row_direction == 'right' %} review-marquee__row--reverse{% endif %}"
    style="--review-marquee-duration: {{ row_duration }}s;"
    data-marquee-row
    data-marquee-speed="{{ row_speed }}"
  >
    <div class="review-marquee__track" data-marquee-track>
      {%- comment -%}
        One loop for both copies rather than two blocks of near-identical markup.
        Only the first copy is real content: the second is hidden from assistive
        tech, and carries no Theme Editor attributes, so a screen reader hears
        each review once and selecting a block in the editor still resolves to a
        single element.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- for copy in (1..2) -%}
        <ul
          class="review-marquee__group"
          data-marquee-group
          {% if copy == 1 %}
            {% if row_label != blank %}
              aria-label="{{ row_label | escape }}"
            {% endif %}
            role="list"
          {% else %}
            data-marquee-clone
            aria-hidden="true"
          {% endif %}
        >
          {%- for review in reviews -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign in_row = true
              if row_map != blank and row_key != blank
                unless row_map[forloop.index0] == row_key
                  assign in_row = false
                endunless
              endif
            -%}
            {%- unless in_row -%}
              {%- continue -%}
            {%- endunless -%}

            {%- liquid
              comment
                Avatars are small, but the handful that are on screen at first
                paint should not wait for the lazy pass.
              endcomment
              assign lazy_avatar = true
              if eager and copy == 1 and forloop.index0 < 4
                assign lazy_avatar = false
              endif
            -%}

            <li
              class="review-marquee__item"
              {% if copy == 1 %}{{ review.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}
            >
              {%- render 'review-card',
                quote: review.settings.quote,
                name: review.settings.name,
                role: review.settings.role,
                avatar: review.settings.avatar,
                avatar_url: review.settings.avatar_url,
                quote_marks: quote_marks,
                clamp: clamp,
                lazy_load: lazy_avatar
              -%}
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
